  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shashikumara G M @ Kumar vs The State Of Karnataka on 24 April, 2024 Author: S Vishwajith Shetty Bench: S Vishwajith Shetty -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:16512 Crl.P No. 853 of 2024 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 24Th Day Of April, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice S Vishwajith Shetty Criminal Petition No. 853 Of 2024 Between: Shashikumara G.M @ Kumar S/O G.S. Manjunatha Aged About 28 Years R/O 28, Uddaghatta Bharamasamudra Dcm Township Davanagere - 577 528. ...Petitioner (By Sri. Bhadravadi Siddeswara.,Advocate) And: 1. The State Of Karnataka By Azad Nagar P.S Davanagere District Digitally Rep By The Spp signed by High Court Premises Pavithra N Location: Bengaluru City - 560 001. High Court of Karnataka 2. Sri Ravisivamurthy Hipparagi Food And Civil Supply Dept.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. Heard the learned Counsel for the parties. 3. Learned Counsel for the petitioner having reiterated the grounds urged in the petition submits that the sample of the seized rice was forwarded to the Food Corporation of India for the purpose of examination and also for issuing a report. He submits that the Food Corporation of India has returned the NC: 2024:KHC:16512 rice sample vide its letter dated 12.07.2021, and therefore, no purpose would be served in continuing the impugned proceedings. He submits that the Trial Court without appreciating this aspect of the matter, has erred in taking cognizance of the charge sheeted offences. 4. Learned HCGP has opposed the petition. However, he does not dispute that the sample of the rice referred to the Food Corporation of India, has been returned on the ground that it is not possible to classify/categorize the same.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. Heard the learned Counsel for the parties. 3. Learned Counsel for the petitioner having reiterated the grounds urged in the petition submits that the sample of the seized rice was forwarded to the Food Corporation of India for the purpose of examination and also for issuing a report. He submits that the Food Corporation of India has returned the NC: 2024:KHC:16512 rice sample vide its letter dated 12.07.2021, and therefore, no purpose would be served in continuing the impugned proceedings. He submits that the Trial Court without appreciating this aspect of the matter, has erred in taking cognizance of the charge sheeted offences.",
    "respondent_arguments": "4. Learned HCGP has opposed the petition. However, he does not dispute that the sample of the rice referred to the Food Corporation of India, has been returned on the ground that it is not possible to classify/categorize the same.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
